  "evidence": "The not_null test on stg_lineitem_extended_price failed with 29,778 nulls. In raw.lineitem there are exactly 29,778 rows where l_returnflag <> 'N' (non_N_rows). The stg_lineitem model defines extended_price as `case when l_returnflag = 'N' then l_extendedprice end`, which intentionally produces nulls for those rows. The upstream raw data has no nulls in l_extendedprice, and the row counts match (total 60,175 rows, 30,397 N rows with non‑null extended_price, 29,778 nulls). Therefore the issue originates from the model's SQL logic, not the source data. Fix by patching stg_lineitem to set `extended_price = l_extendedprice` (or adjust the condition) so the column is never null, satisfying the not_null test."
}
